{"record": "end", "run_id": "20261116T081748Z_dev-05_flat_8a97", "reason": "answered", "detail": "", "answer": {"answer": "The paper does not give a detection significance for the GCE, in σ or as a test statistic. The 17.7-year analysis fits GCE spectra and DM annihilation regions, and the fitted GCE flux stays nonzero in all 80 diffuse-emission models. The text says this observation alone does not establish its statistical significance. The only statistics it reports are fit χ² values of the DM spectra to the GCE spectrum, for example χ²_min = 27.50 for 12 degrees of freedom for b b̄. These are goodness-of-fit numbers, not a detection significance.", "found": false, "evidence": [{"arxiv_id": "2610.26648v1", "section_id": "3.5"}, {"arxiv_id": "2610.26648v1", "section_id": "3.4"}, {"arxiv_id": "2610.26648v1", "section_id": "6.1"}]}, "turns": 2, "seconds": 4.485, "tool_calls": 1, "tool_result_chars": 147086, "input_tokens": 6, "output_tokens": 419, "cache_creation_input_tokens": 65487, "cache_read_input_tokens": 1840, "parser_versions": ["4"], "response_models": ["claude-sonnet-5-5"], "ended_at": "2026-11-16T08:17:53+00:00"}
